# Implementation Steps

## Step 1: Launch EC2 Instance

- Launch an Amazon Linux 2023 EC2 instance.
- Configure Security Group to allow:
  - SSH (22)
  - HTTP (80)

Install Apache Web Server.

```bash
sudo yum update -y
sudo yum install httpd -y
sudo systemctl start httpd
sudo systemctl enable httpd

echo "<h1>AWS Cloud Engineer Project</h1>" | sudo tee /var/www/html/index.html
```

---

## Step 2: Create IAM Role

Create an IAM Role for EC2.

Attach the following policy:

- CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy

Attach the IAM Role to the EC2 instance.

---

## Step 3: Create Launch Template

Configure:

- Amazon Linux 2023 AMI
- t2.micro
- Security Group
- IAM Role

User Data:

```bash
#!/bin/bash
yum update -y
yum install httpd -y
systemctl start httpd
systemctl enable httpd

echo "<h1>Server Created by Auto Scaling</h1>" > /var/www/html/index.html
```

---

## Step 4: Create Target Group

Configuration:

- Target Type: Instance
- Protocol: HTTP
- Port: 80

Register the EC2 instance.

---

## Step 5: Create Application Load Balancer

Configuration:

- Internet Facing
- HTTP Listener (Port 80)
- Attach Target Group

Use the Load Balancer DNS Name to access the application.

---

## Step 6: Create Auto Scaling Group

Configuration:

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Desired Capacity | 2 |
| Minimum Capacity | 2 |
| Maximum Capacity | 5 |

Attach the Launch Template and Target Group.

---

## Step 7: Configure Auto Scaling Policy

Target Tracking Policy

Metric:

- Average CPU Utilization

Target:

- 70%

Scaling Behavior:

- CPU > 70% → Launch one EC2 instance
- CPU < 20% → Terminate one EC2 instance

---

## Step 8: Configure CloudWatch

Create the following alarms:

- High CPU Utilization
- Instance Status Check Failed

Monitor:

- CPU Utilization
- Instance Health
- Auto Scaling Events

---

## Step 9: Configure Amazon SNS

Create an SNS Topic.

Topic Name:

```
CloudAlerts
```

Subscribe your email address.

CloudWatch Alarm → SNS Topic → Email Notification

---

## Step 10: Configure AWS CloudTrail

Create a Trail.

Trail Name:

```
CloudEngineerTrail
```

Store logs in an Amazon S3 bucket.

Track:

- EC2 Launch
- EC2 Termination
- IAM Changes
- Security Group Changes
- Auto Scaling Activities

---

# Testing

## Test 1: Application Load Balancer

Stop one EC2 instance.

Expected Result:

- Load Balancer routes requests only to healthy instances.
- Application remains available.

---

## Test 2: Auto Scaling

Install Stress.

```bash
sudo yum install stress -y
```

Generate CPU Load.

```bash
stress --cpu 2 --timeout 300
```

Expected Result:

- CPU utilization exceeds 70%.
- CloudWatch Alarm is triggered.
- Auto Scaling launches a new EC2 instance.

---

## Test 3: SNS Notification

Trigger a CloudWatch Alarm.

Expected Result:

- Email notification is received.

---

## Test 4: CloudTrail

Terminate an EC2 instance.

Verify:

- User Name
- Event Time
- Source IP
- AWS API Called

