# Sample Scenarios

## Scenario 1: High Traffic

- CPU utilization exceeds 70%.
- CloudWatch Alarm is triggered.
- Auto Scaling launches a new EC2 instance.
- Load Balancer distributes traffic across healthy instances.

---

## Scenario 2: EC2 Failure

- One EC2 instance becomes unhealthy.
- Load Balancer removes it from service.
- Auto Scaling launches a replacement instance.
- Application remains available.

---

## Scenario 3: IAM Change

- An IAM policy or role is modified.
- CloudTrail records the event.
- Security administrators can identify:
  - Who performed the action
  - When it occurred
  - Source IP Address
  - AWS API Used

---

# CloudWatch vs CloudTrail

| CloudWatch | CloudTrail |
|------------|------------|
| Monitoring Service | Auditing Service |
| Collects Metrics | Records AWS API Calls |
| Creates Alarms | Tracks User Activities |
| Monitors Resources | Supports Compliance |
| Integrates with SNS | Maintains Audit History |

